      "content": "That's a bit better, but the score is still hovering around 0.78. It's not quite hitting that 0.85 threshold we need for the premium donor segment.\n\nIt looks like the sentiment tool is struggling with the \"bleached and worn\" and \"heartbreaking\" parts—it's probably flagging those as too negative, even though they are factual. Could you try to pivot the language so it's even more focused on the \"hope,\" \"beauty,\" and \"triumph\" of the restoration? I really want to push that positivity score up without crossing into being a cartoon, but we need to make sure the tool sees it as an overwhelmingly positive/inspiring message. \n\nTry to find a way to layer in more uplifting, high-sentiment words so the tool recognizes the \"hopeful\" intent of the letter. Can you take another pass?",
